WEBVTT

00:06.923 --> 00:08.925
[wind blowing]

00:11.052 --> 00:13.847
[calm flute music]

00:16.975 --> 00:18.977
[distant metal rattling]

00:23.606 --> 00:25.608
[rattling continues]

00:26.943 --> 00:29.237
[Usagi grunting]

00:31.322 --> 00:33.324
[panting]

00:42.000 --> 00:43.835
[gasps]

00:44.544 --> 00:46.588
[breathing heavily]

00:49.632 --> 00:52.510
[Shigenori]
Focus on what you're doing, Yuzuha!

00:52.594 --> 00:53.887
[panting]

00:55.180 --> 00:57.182
[tender piano music]

00:57.265 --> 00:58.391
[exhales deeply]

01:04.606 --> 01:06.608
[tender music continues]

01:11.029 --> 01:12.072
It's okay, Dad.

01:12.864 --> 01:14.866
[distant laser blasting]

01:17.452 --> 01:19.454
[lasers zapping]

01:21.164 --> 01:22.457
I'm gonna survive.

01:24.334 --> 01:26.336
[ominous music]

01:31.341 --> 01:33.343
[theme music]

02:39.450 --> 02:41.452
[soft music]

02:52.463 --> 02:55.884
SHIBUYA STATION

02:56.926 --> 03:00.138
[crows cawing]

03:11.190 --> 03:13.818
[ignition key clicking]

03:17.739 --> 03:18.656
What?

03:20.158 --> 03:21.075
[sighs]

03:29.125 --> 03:30.168
[groans]

03:30.668 --> 03:31.711
[sighs]

03:44.974 --> 03:46.017
[coughs]

03:49.520 --> 03:50.521
[slams]

03:54.943 --> 03:55.985
[Arisu] How did it go?

03:56.069 --> 03:57.695
[Chota] Not good. Ugh, I got nothing.

03:58.696 --> 03:59.572
[Karube] All right.

04:00.073 --> 04:02.700
Let's just grab anything
that might be useful.

04:04.827 --> 04:08.748
[distant clattering]

04:14.545 --> 04:16.839
FURNITURE AND INTERIOR GOODS FLOOR

04:16.923 --> 04:18.466
[Chota sighs]
Just as I thought,

04:18.549 --> 04:20.760
all the IC chips have been destroyed.

04:23.388 --> 04:25.265
Video cameras, digital clocks.

04:25.848 --> 04:28.226
Anything that operates
with an electronic circuit board

04:28.309 --> 04:29.560
isn't gonna work.

04:32.021 --> 04:34.232
But old stuff like this still works,

04:34.816 --> 04:37.235
since none of it has any IC chips.

04:37.318 --> 04:39.988
[radio static]

04:40.071 --> 04:41.239
[Arisu] What does that mean?

04:42.991 --> 04:44.826
It might mean…

04:45.785 --> 04:46.828
Hurry!

04:46.911 --> 04:48.705
- [Karube shouts]
- [Chota] Look, fireworks!

04:48.788 --> 04:50.123
[lights clunk]

04:53.418 --> 04:55.712
An electromagnetic pulse attack.

04:57.422 --> 04:59.465
[Chota] I read about this online.

04:59.549 --> 05:01.509
When inserted into the stratosphere,

05:01.592 --> 05:05.638
it's a weapon capable of destroying
the electronics in an entire city.

05:06.931 --> 05:08.016
Seriously?

05:08.099 --> 05:10.393
[soft unsettling music]

05:13.604 --> 05:16.357
So… why is this working?

05:16.441 --> 05:18.526
[breathes deeply]

05:18.609 --> 05:19.986
No idea.

05:22.405 --> 05:23.406
VISA
RYOHEI ARISU

05:23.489 --> 05:24.407
REMAINING DAYS: 3

05:25.158 --> 05:26.242
[Arisu] Hey!

05:35.918 --> 05:37.128
[sighs]

05:38.629 --> 05:41.132
It's completely useless
if we can't charge it.

05:41.716 --> 05:42.717
[thuds]

05:46.554 --> 05:48.765
[Karube] This place looks safe enough.

05:52.226 --> 05:54.228
[metal clanking]

05:54.312 --> 05:55.354
[knife zings]

05:57.607 --> 05:59.692
All right. This might be a good weapon.

06:00.860 --> 06:03.196
- What do you need a weapon for?
- [Karube exhales deeply]

06:05.406 --> 06:06.491
Zombies.

06:07.325 --> 06:09.327
[laughs wryly]

06:11.871 --> 06:13.831
You know you can't use
electricity or gas, right?

06:14.457 --> 06:16.250
But I can still use the portable stove.

06:16.334 --> 06:18.628
It has batteries
that I can also use in my flashlight.

06:18.711 --> 06:20.463
And I like a hot meal sometimes.

06:21.923 --> 06:22.882
[Shibuki] Hmm.

06:22.965 --> 06:26.594
["Hang On Sloopy" by the McCoys playing]

06:27.762 --> 06:30.681
♪ Hang on, Sloopy ♪

06:30.765 --> 06:32.892
♪ Sloopy, hang on ♪

06:32.975 --> 06:34.060
[Karube exhales sharply]

06:36.062 --> 06:38.940
♪ Hang on, Sloopy ♪

06:39.023 --> 06:41.109
♪ Sloopy, hang on ♪

06:42.610 --> 06:44.112
[slurping]

06:45.196 --> 06:46.572
- [exhales softly]
- [Chota] This is so good!

06:47.740 --> 06:49.534
[Karube] Ah, nice and hot!

06:49.617 --> 06:51.661
[Chota] We haven't eaten anything
since yesterday.

06:51.744 --> 06:53.955
[Karube exhales in pleasure]

06:54.580 --> 06:57.083
Hey, what were you guys doing

06:57.166 --> 06:58.709
when everyone disappeared?

07:00.920 --> 07:01.963
Bathroom.

07:02.588 --> 07:04.423
We were all in the same stall.

07:05.049 --> 07:06.843
Why were you all in the same stall?

07:07.426 --> 07:08.344
Where were you?

07:09.929 --> 07:11.931
- [Shibuki moans]
- [man breathes heavily]

07:13.516 --> 07:14.725
Saori…

07:14.809 --> 07:16.727
- [smooches]
- [Shibuki moans]

07:17.895 --> 07:19.981
[moaning continues]

07:24.026 --> 07:25.111
I was at work.

07:26.487 --> 07:29.282
I was in the conference room
doing some paperwork.

07:30.032 --> 07:31.117
And then,

07:31.742 --> 07:33.703
everyone in the office disappeared.

07:34.662 --> 07:37.415
Did you happen to see or hear
anything at all?

07:39.750 --> 07:41.752
[splattering]

07:45.882 --> 07:47.425
- [lights clunk]
- [water slows]

07:56.809 --> 07:57.768
[Shibuki] Boss?

08:01.397 --> 08:03.399
[soft eerie music]

08:14.869 --> 08:15.995
Not really.

08:17.747 --> 08:19.540
I came to this place three days ago,

08:20.750 --> 08:24.170
and I was forced to play this game,
just like all of you were.

08:26.005 --> 08:28.382
Everybody died, except for me.

08:31.093 --> 08:32.803
You mean, you used them as bait, right?

08:32.887 --> 08:34.472
Think whatever you want.

08:35.973 --> 08:37.308
All I wanted…

08:38.893 --> 08:40.394
was to survive.

08:48.069 --> 08:49.362
[sighs]

08:51.531 --> 08:52.698
Well…

08:55.034 --> 08:57.036
[Karube gulping]

09:00.373 --> 09:01.832
What kind of game was it?

09:05.253 --> 09:06.754
It was at the subway.

09:08.881 --> 09:10.841
They used poisonous gas in the game.

09:13.719 --> 09:15.096
Everyone was vomiting blood.

09:16.764 --> 09:18.474
Blood was coming out of their eyes.

09:23.271 --> 09:24.313
Weird, huh?

09:24.397 --> 09:26.065
[utensils clattering]

09:26.148 --> 09:28.109
[Arisu] The day everyone disappeared.

09:28.192 --> 09:29.860
It was yesterday for the three of us.

09:29.944 --> 09:30.945
[Chota] Yeah.

09:31.028 --> 09:32.989
But it was three days ago for her.

09:33.072 --> 09:34.323
Why the time difference?

09:34.991 --> 09:35.825
That's right.

09:36.325 --> 09:38.202
And those vegetables that were rotten…

09:38.911 --> 09:41.038
They take longer than a few days
to go bad.

09:41.831 --> 09:43.165
What's going on?

09:45.293 --> 09:47.044
Maybe the speed of time is…

09:47.587 --> 09:49.046
different from the normal world?

09:49.755 --> 09:50.590
Huh?

09:51.382 --> 09:53.134
I don't really know, but…

09:53.843 --> 09:56.554
Take the, the four of us here.

09:57.263 --> 10:01.267
The timeline of when people disappeared
is different, like you said.

10:02.143 --> 10:03.352
[sighs]

10:04.103 --> 10:07.898
Did we time travel while we were
in the subway bathroom stall?

10:07.982 --> 10:09.483
There's no way.

10:09.567 --> 10:11.444
There's also no way
people just disappeared.

10:11.527 --> 10:12.737
Time travel isn't real.

10:12.820 --> 10:14.572
Then explain the game
and people disappearing.

10:14.655 --> 10:16.073
- [thuds]
- I don't know, all right?

10:16.157 --> 10:17.450
[Arisu] Anyways,

10:17.533 --> 10:20.077
one thing we know for sure
about this game…

10:21.829 --> 10:23.623
A game master's running it.

10:24.290 --> 10:25.416
Game master?

10:26.208 --> 10:27.877
Someone came up with this game.

10:28.544 --> 10:29.795
That's for sure.

10:30.463 --> 10:31.505
[sighs]

10:31.589 --> 10:33.758
So while we're in a bathroom stall,

10:33.841 --> 10:36.177
they get rid of everyone in Tokyo

10:36.260 --> 10:37.720
and set up this game?

10:37.803 --> 10:39.263
They keep track of our movements…

10:40.097 --> 10:41.015
[laser zaps]

10:41.098 --> 10:43.851
…and fire lasers through our heads
when we make the wrong move.

10:45.353 --> 10:47.647
[sighs]
What kind of person would do that?

10:48.773 --> 10:50.441
I don't know, but it's definitely possible

10:50.524 --> 10:52.818
if they inserted
a highly accurate GPS microchip

10:52.902 --> 10:53.986
into our bodies.

10:54.070 --> 10:56.614
[scoffs]
Spoken like a real IT geek.

10:57.156 --> 10:59.825
But who the hell could be
behind this thing?

10:59.909 --> 11:01.118
- [Karube sighs]
- [Shibuki] Hmm.

11:01.202 --> 11:02.411
Could it be…

11:02.912 --> 11:05.998
some government-run experiment
or something?

11:08.084 --> 11:10.836
There were some rumors
going around at my work.

11:11.837 --> 11:14.590
An IT company from Europe wanted
to conduct an experiment.

11:14.674 --> 11:16.467
They'd established a VR space,

11:16.550 --> 11:19.678
then created an alternate world
identical to the real one.

11:22.890 --> 11:25.726
But we should be able to tell VR
from the real world.

11:26.936 --> 11:28.437
[Chota] Man…

11:28.521 --> 11:29.897
This hurts.

11:31.440 --> 11:33.401
I don't think
VR can cause burns like that.

11:33.484 --> 11:34.777
[Chota groans]

11:35.861 --> 11:38.072
Maybe it's God.
[breathes shakily]

11:38.155 --> 11:40.491
This has to be the work of God.

11:40.574 --> 11:42.701
Otherwise, how else do you explain it?

11:42.785 --> 11:44.787
- [grunts]
- You're talking crazy now.

11:45.454 --> 11:46.956
No, man. I think…

11:47.832 --> 11:49.291
God really does exist.

11:51.043 --> 11:52.545
[Chota groans, grunts]

11:53.838 --> 11:56.173
Hey, is it getting worse?

11:56.257 --> 11:58.509
[Chota breathing shakily]

11:58.592 --> 11:59.844
[Chota] It's all right.

11:59.927 --> 12:00.970
Oh, it's gonna be fine.

12:02.179 --> 12:03.848
[Chota groaning]

12:05.307 --> 12:07.309
[somber music]

12:08.644 --> 12:10.896
[Arisu] I think we gotta get Chota
to a doctor.

12:13.190 --> 12:14.650
You know how he is.

12:15.276 --> 12:17.153
It's probably hurting more than he says.

12:17.653 --> 12:18.654
But it's getting to him.

12:22.408 --> 12:23.367
[Karube] Arisu.

12:24.869 --> 12:27.496
[Karube sighs]
Let's get in the game tomorrow night,

12:27.580 --> 12:28.664
just you and me.

12:29.665 --> 12:30.583
What?

12:31.584 --> 12:33.794
But we've got three days left
on our visas.

12:34.503 --> 12:35.754
[Karube sighs]

12:35.838 --> 12:38.799
It's better to get in the game
while we still have time.

12:40.217 --> 12:41.760
I just don't think

12:41.844 --> 12:45.556
Chota's gonna be able to make it through.
He's in too much pain.

12:48.017 --> 12:50.352
[breathing heavily]

12:51.604 --> 12:52.688
[groaning]

12:52.771 --> 12:53.981
[Shibuki] How are you doing?

12:54.982 --> 12:56.108
Not bad, thanks.

12:57.568 --> 13:00.529
[Karube] If the two of us don't figure out
how to get through this game,

13:00.613 --> 13:02.239
we won't be able to protect Chota.

13:02.323 --> 13:04.033
[water sloshing]

13:04.116 --> 13:05.117
[Arisu] You're right, but…

13:06.785 --> 13:08.162
Maybe we can find a doctor too.

13:08.662 --> 13:10.456
We'll meet more people if we're playing.

13:12.541 --> 13:14.418
[Arisu] Do we really have to play again?

13:15.044 --> 13:17.087
Maybe we'll get an idea
what this game's about.

13:17.713 --> 13:18.756
[Arisu sighs exasperatedly]

13:22.843 --> 13:23.928
[Arisu] Yeah, I guess.

13:24.970 --> 13:26.096
If we play,

13:26.180 --> 13:27.973
we might find out their signature.

13:29.934 --> 13:31.060
Signature?

13:32.019 --> 13:34.063
Yeah. If someone actually created
this game,

13:35.731 --> 13:39.026
there's a kind of signature they use,
like formatting.

13:39.944 --> 13:41.070
If we can discover that,

13:41.612 --> 13:43.948
we might be able to figure out
a strategy for the game.

13:45.115 --> 13:47.117
[breathes deeply]

13:49.995 --> 13:50.996
[lights click]

13:51.956 --> 13:53.958
[bold music]

14:04.134 --> 14:09.390
TOEI SENDAGAYA APARTMENT

14:23.070 --> 14:25.072
[soft unsettling music]

14:34.540 --> 14:35.624
[sighs]

14:37.793 --> 14:40.254
1 PER PERSON

14:41.046 --> 14:43.507
FACE RECOGNITION IN PROGRESS
PLEASE WAIT FOR A MOMENT

14:43.591 --> 14:46.385
[announcer]
Please wait until the game commences.

14:46.468 --> 14:48.888
There are currently ten participants.

14:48.971 --> 14:51.640
One minute until registration closes.

14:52.975 --> 14:54.935
Um, excuse me.

14:55.019 --> 14:58.230
Wha-- Where did all the people
in Tokyo go?

15:03.611 --> 15:04.778
This thing here--

15:04.862 --> 15:07.531
[Karube] There's a lot of people here.
Maybe one's a doctor.

15:07.615 --> 15:09.825
[tense music]

15:13.704 --> 15:15.331
1 PER PERSON

15:15.414 --> 15:17.374
[phones chime]

15:32.431 --> 15:34.683
[faint music playing on stereo]

15:41.732 --> 15:43.943
[phone chiming]

15:44.026 --> 15:46.195
[announcer] Registration has closed.

15:46.779 --> 15:52.034
There are a total of 13 participants.
The game will now commence.

15:52.826 --> 15:54.411
[Tatta] E-- Excuse me.

15:54.495 --> 15:57.122
What is this? I was brought here.
[chuckles nervously]

15:57.206 --> 15:59.833
And I… I don't know what's going on.

16:00.918 --> 16:02.836
- It's a game.
- Shut up.

16:03.504 --> 16:05.381
Newbies will slow us down.

16:06.423 --> 16:07.675
They might hate us,

16:08.592 --> 16:10.970
but I think it'd be a good idea
to do what Shibuki did.

16:13.555 --> 16:16.558
[announcer] Difficulty, Five of Spades.

16:16.642 --> 16:18.936
[sinister music]

16:20.688 --> 16:22.022
Five of Spades?

16:22.648 --> 16:24.400
[Nitobe] It's gonna be physical.

16:24.483 --> 16:26.110
Only the strong survive.

16:26.610 --> 16:28.195
I'm Nitobe. Nice to meet you.

16:29.446 --> 16:31.407
The suit means something?

16:31.490 --> 16:32.950
Exactly.
[chuckles]

16:33.909 --> 16:37.121
The suit of the playing card usually means
what kind of game it's gonna be.

16:37.871 --> 16:40.749
Clubs is a team battle.
Diamonds is your wits.

16:40.833 --> 16:41.959
And as for Hearts…

16:43.502 --> 16:45.129
That's the worst one.
[giggles]

16:45.796 --> 16:47.047
- Why is that?
- [Nitobe] Huh?

16:48.007 --> 16:50.759
Because you're playing
with people's hearts then tear them apart.

16:53.804 --> 16:55.097
And the number?

16:55.681 --> 16:56.640
Difficulty.

16:57.808 --> 17:00.519
The higher the number on the card,

17:00.602 --> 17:01.854
the harder it is.

17:02.938 --> 17:03.981
[phone chimes]

17:04.064 --> 17:06.483
[announcer] Game is "Tag".

17:07.526 --> 17:11.155
Rule. Avoid whoever is "it".

17:11.238 --> 17:12.656
[contestants] What?

17:12.740 --> 17:15.784
[all murmuring]

17:17.411 --> 17:20.164
- So who's "it"?
- How should I know?

17:20.247 --> 17:22.166
[announcer] Clear condition.

17:22.249 --> 17:24.293
Discover and touch the symbol

17:24.376 --> 17:27.921
hidden in one of the building's rooms
within the time limit.

17:28.005 --> 17:31.008
You clear the game
when this objective is fulfilled.

17:31.091 --> 17:32.760
Time limit, 20 minutes.

17:34.261 --> 17:35.387
After 20 minutes,

17:35.471 --> 17:39.141
the time bomb hidden
in the building will explode.

17:42.728 --> 17:44.730
[dire music]

17:55.491 --> 17:57.493
TOEI SENDAGAYA APARTMENT

17:57.576 --> 17:59.495
[dire music intensifies]

18:06.418 --> 18:07.669
[Chota] O Holy Mother.

18:08.462 --> 18:11.423
Please forgive us
for all of our mortal sins.

18:12.800 --> 18:14.802
Our smiles are the light of hope.

18:15.844 --> 18:18.263
The Holy Mother will appear when we smile.

18:19.848 --> 18:24.269
O Holy Mother.
Please forgive us for all our mortal sins.

18:25.479 --> 18:27.731
Our smiles are the light of hope.

18:28.273 --> 18:30.734
The Holy Mother will appear when we smile.

18:31.610 --> 18:33.195
[Shibuki] So you believe in God.

18:34.029 --> 18:35.614
[Chota grunts softly]

18:38.283 --> 18:39.118
[Shibuki] Here.

18:41.036 --> 18:44.039
I've also been doing nothing
but praying recently.

18:44.123 --> 18:44.998
[soft chuckle]

18:45.624 --> 18:46.959
I don't believe in God.

18:48.043 --> 18:51.213
But my mother was obsessed
with some cult for a while.

18:51.296 --> 18:52.339
[Shibuki] Hmm.

18:54.258 --> 18:56.260
Because of that, I was bullied in school.

18:56.760 --> 18:58.846
But Arisu and Karube saved me.

19:01.056 --> 19:02.683
They are good friends, aren't they?

19:05.018 --> 19:08.021
Karube is good at fighting
and the girls really love him,

19:08.856 --> 19:12.651
and Arisu is so smart
and comes from a respected family.

19:13.652 --> 19:14.820
[Chota] Then there's me.

19:14.903 --> 19:17.990
My family's poor,
and I'm not really good at anything.

19:18.949 --> 19:23.245
Even now, when I'm hurt and useless,
they're still helping me.

19:25.497 --> 19:26.665
Some people…

19:27.541 --> 19:30.002
like being the strongest ones
in their group.

19:31.044 --> 19:32.504
It makes them feel better.

19:34.047 --> 19:35.424
They're just so different.

19:35.507 --> 19:38.218
Think you might feel good enough
to play the next game?

19:41.680 --> 19:42.973
[Shibuki] How does your leg feel?

19:46.310 --> 19:47.811
They're just so different.

19:47.895 --> 19:51.315
Are you willing to die too,
to save your friends?

19:58.906 --> 20:00.240
[phone chiming]

20:00.324 --> 20:03.493
[announcer]
The game will commence in two minutes.

20:04.620 --> 20:05.787
Stop following us.

20:05.871 --> 20:08.248
[laughs]
Just feeling you guys out.

20:08.332 --> 20:10.584
I'm thinking you two might be
good enough to be my allies.

20:10.667 --> 20:11.919
- Lucky ass.
- [laughs]

20:12.002 --> 20:14.379
- Are you a doctor?
- Nope, real estate agent.

20:15.172 --> 20:17.007
How many times have you played the game?

20:17.090 --> 20:19.551
[Nitobe] Uh… Let's see, maybe five times?

20:20.135 --> 20:21.511
And you've always won?

20:21.595 --> 20:23.347
I guess so, yeah.
[chuckles]

20:24.431 --> 20:26.225
[Mai] Where should I go to hide?

20:26.308 --> 20:27.684
Look, I don't know, all right?

20:28.185 --> 20:29.937
You can only rely on yourself.

20:33.065 --> 20:34.024
[elevator dings]

20:40.364 --> 20:42.366
[sinister music]

20:46.703 --> 20:48.622
If I wanna see where everyone is,

20:49.206 --> 20:50.958
this is the perfect location.

20:57.214 --> 20:59.216
[sinister music continues]

21:05.555 --> 21:06.807
[Chishiya] Yeah.

21:06.890 --> 21:08.934
I got a weird feeling about this.

21:10.394 --> 21:11.395
[scoffs]

21:16.775 --> 21:17.859
Hmm…

21:18.986 --> 21:21.905
Looks like everyone's about to bite it,
just like they always do.

21:23.865 --> 21:27.244
I think, maybe
you've always been screwed over, Shibuki.

21:27.327 --> 21:29.454
You've never met anyone decent.

21:31.540 --> 21:32.791
[Shibuki] You're right.

21:38.338 --> 21:40.132
Isn't it the same way for you?

21:41.133 --> 21:43.135
[ethereal music]

21:44.636 --> 21:46.805
[believers] O Holy Mother…

21:46.888 --> 21:51.059
Please forgive us for all our mortal sins.

21:58.025 --> 21:59.234
No, you're wrong.

22:05.824 --> 22:07.159
[sobs]

22:09.077 --> 22:10.662
[Chota sniffles, weeps]

22:12.789 --> 22:14.207
It must have been rough.

22:16.626 --> 22:19.004
[sobbing]

22:19.087 --> 22:21.590
[suspenseful music]

22:26.094 --> 22:28.138
[suspenseful music builds]

22:36.813 --> 22:38.940
- [Usagi panting]
- [phone chimes]

22:39.024 --> 22:41.610
[announcer] The game will now commence.

22:42.444 --> 22:45.697
The time limit is 20 minutes.

22:45.781 --> 22:47.908
Commence now.

22:47.991 --> 22:50.452
[timer beeping]

22:52.454 --> 22:54.873
The tagger is on the move.

22:58.293 --> 23:01.046
[fanfare music playing]

23:17.604 --> 23:19.606
[breathing nervously]

23:27.823 --> 23:29.116
[elevator dings]

23:33.203 --> 23:36.540
[elevator door opening]

23:48.051 --> 23:50.762
[distant faint footsteps]

24:13.201 --> 24:15.787
[eerie music]

24:19.875 --> 24:21.877
[approaching footsteps]

24:22.460 --> 24:24.045
[breathes nervously]

24:31.178 --> 24:33.597
[breathing shakily]

24:35.015 --> 24:37.475
[panting]

24:38.310 --> 24:39.436
[grunts]

24:39.519 --> 24:43.315
[tagger breathing heavily]

24:44.900 --> 24:47.027
[approaching footsteps]

24:47.110 --> 24:49.446
[Arisu] All right,
let's find a room we can get into.

24:58.830 --> 25:01.416
[grunts]
We gotta get our asses moving!

25:04.669 --> 25:05.545
[sighs]

25:05.629 --> 25:07.881
[eerie music]

25:18.767 --> 25:20.101
[phone chimes]

25:20.810 --> 25:23.063
[announcer] Three minutes have passed.

25:27.025 --> 25:30.779
[heavy breathing in distance]

25:33.448 --> 25:34.783
[gun firing]

25:34.866 --> 25:36.826
[all shudder]

25:39.120 --> 25:40.497
[quietly]
What the hell was that?

26:00.267 --> 26:02.269
- [thuds]
- [gasps]

26:02.352 --> 26:04.521
[panting]

26:05.272 --> 26:07.274
[ominous music]

26:08.400 --> 26:09.317
[Nitobe] He's dead.

26:09.401 --> 26:11.361
[Arisu breathes shakily]

26:23.540 --> 26:27.168
[approaching footsteps]

26:29.045 --> 26:31.047
[ominous music builds]

26:33.216 --> 26:35.677
[ominous music intensifies]

26:36.761 --> 26:39.014
- Arisu!
- [gunshots]

26:40.015 --> 26:41.599
- [Nitobe] Run!
- [Karube] Go, go!

26:41.683 --> 26:42.934
[screaming]

26:43.018 --> 26:43.852
Arisu!

26:43.935 --> 26:44.769
- Run!
- [Nitobe] Outta the way!

26:44.853 --> 26:45.895
- Go down!
- Hurry!

26:45.979 --> 26:46.980
Go, go, go!

26:47.063 --> 26:48.481
[breathing heavily]

26:48.565 --> 26:49.649
Don't look back! Go!

26:50.442 --> 26:51.901
[Nitobe] Move, move!

26:51.985 --> 26:54.154
[Karube] What are you doing? Hey!

26:54.863 --> 26:56.281
[Arisu] Karube, wait!

26:56.990 --> 26:58.366
[Karube] What are you doing?

26:59.117 --> 27:00.201
[Arisu] Get in there.

27:14.382 --> 27:16.384
[retreating footsteps]

27:18.386 --> 27:20.138
[Shibuki] You're a good person, Chota…

27:20.805 --> 27:22.223
I can trust you, can't I?

27:23.016 --> 27:25.018
[sobbing]

27:27.729 --> 27:29.731
[soft music]

27:37.280 --> 27:38.365
When this started,

27:39.908 --> 27:41.868
I was having sex with my boss.

27:45.163 --> 27:46.498
And I hated it.

27:48.750 --> 27:50.794
I thought you said you were working.

27:52.212 --> 27:53.880
I don't trust those guys.

27:54.631 --> 27:56.758
They didn't need to know the truth,
did they?

28:01.513 --> 28:03.598
[soft music continues]

28:07.894 --> 28:08.895
[smooches]

28:17.695 --> 28:18.905
[exhales deeply]

28:18.988 --> 28:20.615
[Shibuki] Since we're both the same,

28:21.491 --> 28:22.826
we should work together.

28:29.165 --> 28:31.626
[somber choral music]

28:47.100 --> 28:48.560
So we can survive…

28:52.313 --> 28:54.065
[whimpering]

28:54.149 --> 28:56.943
[Nitobe screaming]

28:57.986 --> 28:58.987
[gunshots]

28:59.612 --> 29:00.530
[thuds]

29:01.865 --> 29:02.991
Oh, my god!

29:03.074 --> 29:05.368
I can't do this. I can't do this!

29:07.078 --> 29:08.413
[laser zaps]

29:12.500 --> 29:13.460
[thuds]

29:20.800 --> 29:22.969
[solemn organ music]

29:51.706 --> 29:53.833
- [Mai shouting]
- [Aya] Hurry up, Mai!

29:54.459 --> 29:56.461
[heavy breathing]

29:57.712 --> 29:59.339
- [Mai] Aya!
- Get up!

29:59.422 --> 30:00.381
[gunshots]

30:01.758 --> 30:02.884
[Mai] Aya!

30:05.136 --> 30:06.471
[clatters]

30:07.222 --> 30:09.182
I swear to God I'll kill you!

30:09.265 --> 30:11.476
- [gun cocking]
- [Mai] Get away from me!

30:11.559 --> 30:12.769
[whimpers]

30:12.852 --> 30:14.229
- [gunshots]
- [Mai gags]

30:15.480 --> 30:17.482
[solemn organ music]

30:18.316 --> 30:19.359
[smooches]

30:21.861 --> 30:24.322
I told you the truth
because I trust you, Chota.

30:26.157 --> 30:28.159
[uplifting choral music]

30:36.292 --> 30:38.586
[whispers]
O Holy Mother…

30:40.338 --> 30:41.714
Holy Mother…

30:43.258 --> 30:45.426
[believers] O Holy Mother…

30:45.510 --> 30:48.096
The Holy Mother will appear when we smile.

30:49.472 --> 30:50.890
O Holy Mother…

30:52.183 --> 30:54.143
- Please forgive us for…
- Wait for me, okay?

30:54.227 --> 30:55.937
[believers] …our mortal sins.

30:57.021 --> 30:59.649
Our smiles are the light of hope.

31:00.483 --> 31:02.902
The Holy Mother will appear when we smile.

31:04.070 --> 31:05.697
O Holy Mother…

31:06.656 --> 31:10.243
Please forgive us for our mortal sins.

31:10.326 --> 31:11.995
Please accept this.

31:12.078 --> 31:14.539
[believers]
Our smiles are the light of hope.

31:15.456 --> 31:17.959
The Holy Mother will appear when we smile.

31:19.085 --> 31:20.920
[Niko] Very well, this way.

31:21.504 --> 31:25.049
[believers]
O Holy Mother, please forgive us…

31:26.509 --> 31:29.178
The Holy Mother will appear when we smile.

31:30.179 --> 31:32.557
Our smiles are the light of hope.

31:34.350 --> 31:39.147
O Holy Mother,
please forgive us for our mortal sins.

31:39.230 --> 31:41.608
- Come on, let's go.
- We'll all go together.

31:42.275 --> 31:43.484
[believers] O Holy Mother,

31:44.694 --> 31:46.362
please forgive us for…

31:46.446 --> 31:49.073
- [door shuts]
- [believers] …all our mortal sins.

31:50.867 --> 31:52.702
…all our mortal sins.

31:55.788 --> 31:58.291
O Holy Mother.

32:01.586 --> 32:02.670
[Chota] Please.

32:03.463 --> 32:04.881
Save them.

32:06.382 --> 32:08.009
[Karube shuddering]

32:08.092 --> 32:09.761
[Karube whispers]
What are we gonna do, man?

32:10.553 --> 32:12.680
If you've got a solution, now's the time.

32:12.764 --> 32:13.598
[Arisu whispers]
I don't know what to do

32:13.681 --> 32:15.558
against something like that.

32:15.642 --> 32:18.478
- Come on, man. Think.
- [Arisu] Why don't you think of something?

32:18.561 --> 32:19.604
[both gasp]

32:19.687 --> 32:21.689
[Arisu shuddering]

32:32.951 --> 32:35.036
[suspenseful music]

32:38.373 --> 32:39.958
He didn't see us.

32:41.209 --> 32:43.252
His vision is narrowed
because of the mask.

32:44.420 --> 32:45.630
That's his weak point.

32:46.255 --> 32:47.966
This might be a way
to get through the game.

32:50.635 --> 32:52.971
[loud footsteps]

32:53.054 --> 32:54.931
- Everyone! He's up here!
- [Karube] Hey!

32:55.014 --> 32:56.975
Over here, he's on the second level!

32:57.058 --> 32:58.935
- You'll get us killed!
- He can't see properly

32:59.018 --> 33:00.228
because of his mask!

33:00.311 --> 33:02.313
Tell us where he is if you see him,

33:02.397 --> 33:04.190
and let's all look for the symbol!

33:05.775 --> 33:06.651
[sighs]

33:07.235 --> 33:08.736
That's a good idea, but…

33:09.696 --> 33:11.406
nobody wants to help.

33:11.489 --> 33:13.449
[breathes shakily]

33:16.077 --> 33:18.955
He's in the fourth-level hallway
in the central building!

33:19.038 --> 33:20.748
Anyone there should get out!

33:22.500 --> 33:23.376
Really?

33:23.459 --> 33:25.003
[panting]

33:25.795 --> 33:27.797
- Hurry, get out of here!
- [Hirai] What?

33:28.381 --> 33:29.674
I'm sorry.

33:29.757 --> 33:31.175
[gunshots]

33:33.386 --> 33:34.262
[Chishiya] Oh, ho.

33:34.804 --> 33:35.680
[firing blast]

33:35.763 --> 33:37.015
A climber?

33:37.640 --> 33:38.766
She's not bad.

33:39.726 --> 33:40.727
TOEI SENDAGAYA APARTMENT

33:40.810 --> 33:41.853
[phone chiming]

33:41.936 --> 33:44.439
[announcer]
The game is over in eight minutes.

33:44.522 --> 33:45.565
[timer beeping]

33:45.648 --> 33:48.901
There are currently seven survivors.

33:49.652 --> 33:52.238
[ticking percussive music]

33:55.658 --> 33:58.453
[tagger breathes deeply]

34:07.170 --> 34:09.172
[percussive music builds]

34:15.011 --> 34:16.596
- [gunshots]
- [yelps]

34:20.099 --> 34:21.059
[whimpers]

34:22.435 --> 34:25.855
- [rapid gunshots]
- [both panting]

34:28.733 --> 34:30.777
- [gunshots]
- [Tatta whimpers]

34:32.653 --> 34:34.489
- [whimpering continues]
- Hey! Yo!

34:35.073 --> 34:37.283
Over here! Hey!

34:37.366 --> 34:39.368
[sobs]

34:40.203 --> 34:42.205
[groans]

34:42.789 --> 34:44.582
- [gunshots]
- [yelps]

34:44.665 --> 34:46.375
Leave him! We gotta get outta here!

34:47.210 --> 34:48.753
Come on, man. You can't stay here.

34:48.836 --> 34:50.004
- Move!
- [both grunt]

34:50.088 --> 34:51.422
[gunshots]

34:52.757 --> 34:53.841
Hurry up!

34:53.925 --> 34:56.052
[Arisu and Tatta grunting]

34:56.135 --> 34:57.220
[gunshots]

34:57.929 --> 34:59.889
[timer beeping]

35:05.520 --> 35:06.771
And here we go.

35:07.563 --> 35:09.565
[all panting]

35:12.860 --> 35:13.861
[Karube] Arisu!

35:14.695 --> 35:16.155
- [panting]
- Hurry!

35:17.073 --> 35:18.241
- Hurry.
- [knife swipes]

35:18.991 --> 35:20.576
This guy's going down now.

35:20.660 --> 35:23.079
What? But he's got a machine gun.

35:23.162 --> 35:25.248
[Aguni] So? The tagger's human.

35:26.415 --> 35:27.834
[Karube gasps]

35:28.876 --> 35:31.879
He's 190 centimeters tall
and weighs 90 kilos,

35:31.963 --> 35:33.214
and he's right-handed.

35:33.297 --> 35:35.383
[Aguni] He's a pretty good shot, too.

35:35.466 --> 35:38.219
Probably military or law enforcement.

35:38.302 --> 35:39.554
[Jin pants]
Aguni!

35:40.346 --> 35:41.430
Here it is.

35:48.604 --> 35:49.814
Use this.

35:56.195 --> 35:57.446
Let's get this guy.

36:01.325 --> 36:02.952
You, go look for the symbol.

36:04.078 --> 36:04.912
[Karube] What?

36:05.788 --> 36:08.249
Hey! Why should we do what you say?

36:08.332 --> 36:09.417
I got it.

36:09.500 --> 36:10.501
I'll go up to the top.

36:11.961 --> 36:12.879
[Karube] Arisu!

36:13.379 --> 36:14.547
I don't like this.

36:14.630 --> 36:16.174
- There's no other choice.
- [landing thud]

36:16.257 --> 36:17.925
[Usagi] I checked
the south side of the fifth floor,

36:18.009 --> 36:19.802
and the south and east side
of the sixth floor.

36:19.886 --> 36:22.221
[panting]
Let's split up and find the symbol.

36:23.181 --> 36:24.932
I didn't check
the first and second floors.

36:25.016 --> 36:27.560
All right. I'll go check.
[grunts]

36:27.643 --> 36:29.145
- [Arisu] Hey!
- [Karube] Hey!

36:35.735 --> 36:37.862
It's time to take this guy out.

36:37.945 --> 36:39.989
[suspenseful music]

36:41.949 --> 36:42.909
[phone chimes]

36:42.992 --> 36:45.745
[announcer]
Five minutes remaining in the game.

36:47.705 --> 36:48.706
See you later.

36:49.790 --> 36:50.791
Yeah.

36:59.342 --> 37:01.302
[breathing shakily]

37:07.892 --> 37:09.852
[Arisu] Where the hell is that symbol?

37:09.936 --> 37:11.896
[panting]

37:15.066 --> 37:17.818
Calm down. Relax and think.

37:18.861 --> 37:20.821
[Jin panting]

37:22.281 --> 37:24.784
[heavy footsteps]

37:24.867 --> 37:26.702
Come on, follow me.

37:27.245 --> 37:28.746
[breathing rapidly]

37:28.829 --> 37:30.873
He's using a MAC-10.

37:30.957 --> 37:33.918
He can go through a 32-round clip
in 1.5 seconds.

37:35.711 --> 37:37.755
[Aguni]
We'll take him when he's reloading.

37:37.838 --> 37:39.840
[action music]

37:39.924 --> 37:41.092
[approaching footsteps]

37:42.718 --> 37:43.844
[Jin sighs]

37:46.055 --> 37:47.181
[shouts]
I'm right here!

37:50.518 --> 37:52.687
That's right. Come on!

37:53.562 --> 37:55.606
[suspenseful music]

38:01.821 --> 38:02.863
Aguni?

38:02.947 --> 38:04.573
[Jin breathes nervously]

38:05.449 --> 38:06.325
Aguni?

38:06.409 --> 38:08.119
[shouts]
Aguni!

38:08.202 --> 38:09.328
[gunshots]

38:09.412 --> 38:11.205
[Jin gags]

38:11.706 --> 38:12.707
[gunshots]

38:12.790 --> 38:13.958
[whispers]
Son of a bitch.

38:14.041 --> 38:16.252
[ominous music intensifies]

38:17.712 --> 38:18.671
[gasps]

38:19.547 --> 38:21.632
- [grunts]
- [aerosol whooshes]

38:21.716 --> 38:23.175
[continuous gunshots]

38:25.720 --> 38:26.887
[trigger clicks]

38:26.971 --> 38:28.306
[gun cocks]

38:28.389 --> 38:31.142
[Karube yells, panting]

38:34.562 --> 38:36.063
- [Karube grunts]
- [canister clangs]

38:36.147 --> 38:37.732
[Aguni screams]

38:37.815 --> 38:39.984
- [thwacking]
- [grunting]

38:46.157 --> 38:47.074
[thuds]

38:47.158 --> 38:49.243
[coughs, chokes]

38:50.328 --> 38:51.787
- [whacks]
- [grunts]

38:53.956 --> 38:54.999
[shouts]

38:55.624 --> 38:58.294
[grunting]

38:59.503 --> 39:01.213
- [groans]
- [clanks]

39:01.297 --> 39:03.049
[groaning]

39:04.050 --> 39:04.967
[blade scrapes]

39:07.178 --> 39:09.388
[menacing music]

39:09.472 --> 39:11.098
[blade zinging]

39:11.974 --> 39:13.184
[gasps]

39:14.060 --> 39:15.186
[yelps]

39:15.269 --> 39:16.687
[blood spattering]

39:17.438 --> 39:20.066
[Karube groaning]

39:23.069 --> 39:24.445
[screams]

39:25.988 --> 39:27.281
[groans]

39:27.990 --> 39:29.241
[swooshes]

39:30.951 --> 39:32.870
[grunts]

39:32.953 --> 39:34.121
[groans in pain]

39:35.539 --> 39:37.500
[Arisu panting]

39:40.419 --> 39:41.337
Come on.

39:42.004 --> 39:43.130
Think, dammit.

39:43.214 --> 39:45.049
[panting]

39:48.219 --> 39:50.221
[shuddering]

39:58.020 --> 39:59.271
- [gunshots]
- [yelps]

40:02.650 --> 40:05.736
Why would he shoot from so far away?

40:06.237 --> 40:08.614
[breathing heavily]

40:08.697 --> 40:10.699
[suspenseful music]

40:15.538 --> 40:16.539
[exclaims]

40:16.622 --> 40:18.082
[approaching footsteps]

40:21.085 --> 40:22.378
Figured it out too, huh?

40:23.546 --> 40:25.756
[Arisu] Yeah, the symbol's in here.

40:26.257 --> 40:28.259
[suspenseful music builds]

40:34.515 --> 40:35.850
Gonna open it?

40:37.351 --> 40:38.978
Why was he chasing us?

40:40.146 --> 40:41.647
He could've just waited.

40:43.441 --> 40:45.276
Guess there's something we don't know.

40:47.945 --> 40:48.779
[Chishiya] Except,

40:49.280 --> 40:50.322
not much time left.

40:51.198 --> 40:53.576
[suspenseful music]

40:53.659 --> 40:54.827
[heavy breathing]

40:54.910 --> 40:56.370
[phone chimes]

40:56.454 --> 40:59.123
[announcer]
Three minutes remaining in the game.

41:04.503 --> 41:06.547
[doorknob cranks]

41:08.966 --> 41:10.968
[door creaks]

41:45.586 --> 41:47.630
[suspenseful music]

41:48.964 --> 41:49.798
[shouts]
Look out!

41:49.882 --> 41:51.383
[gunshots]

41:51.467 --> 41:52.927
[taser crackling]

41:53.010 --> 41:53.886
[thuds]

41:53.969 --> 41:56.472
[panting]

41:59.350 --> 42:00.392
[sighs]

42:01.352 --> 42:02.770
It never hurts to be prepared--

42:02.853 --> 42:04.688
[gunshots]

42:04.772 --> 42:06.440
[door clunks, slams]

42:07.107 --> 42:08.484
[gunshots]

42:09.235 --> 42:10.861
[lights flick]

42:10.945 --> 42:13.364
[doorknob rattling]

42:15.491 --> 42:17.034
[Arisu panting]

42:18.536 --> 42:20.454
[panting continues]

42:23.874 --> 42:25.167
PUSH BOTH BUTTONS
AT ONCE TO CLEAR GAME

42:25.251 --> 42:26.168
[Arisu] Damn it!

42:26.877 --> 42:29.964
[Karube breathing heavily, wincing]

42:31.507 --> 42:33.050
[Arisu shouts]
Someone get over here!

42:33.133 --> 42:36.637
The symbol's up here! Room 406!

42:36.720 --> 42:37.596
[gasps]

42:38.180 --> 42:39.765
[Arisu] I can't clear the game alone!

42:39.848 --> 42:42.017
We need two people to do it!

42:42.101 --> 42:44.144
Seriously?

42:44.728 --> 42:46.313
[shouts]
Arisu!

42:46.397 --> 42:48.732
[groaning]

42:48.816 --> 42:50.526
[Aguni grunts]

42:52.903 --> 42:55.322
[groaning]

42:58.367 --> 43:00.077
[strains]

43:00.995 --> 43:02.538
[canister clanging]

43:04.039 --> 43:06.041
[tense music]

43:11.213 --> 43:13.132
Now we're having fun, aren't we?

43:14.049 --> 43:16.135
[bullets blasting]

43:18.304 --> 43:19.179
[slams]

43:22.766 --> 43:23.601
[phone chimes]

43:23.684 --> 43:26.520
[announcer]
One minute remaining in the game.

43:28.063 --> 43:29.231
[exhales deeply]

43:31.483 --> 43:32.776
[gunshots]

43:32.860 --> 43:33.736
[Arisu grunts]

43:33.819 --> 43:35.946
[suspenseful music]

43:36.030 --> 43:37.698
[gunshots]

43:38.699 --> 43:40.659
[grunting]

43:44.204 --> 43:45.789
[shouts]
Someone!

43:45.873 --> 43:47.333
Help me!
[grunts]

43:47.416 --> 43:48.334
[thuds]

43:48.876 --> 43:50.586
[grunts angrily]

43:55.841 --> 43:57.801
[thwacking]

43:57.885 --> 43:59.845
- [straining]
- [gunshots]

44:01.597 --> 44:04.642
[announcer]
30 seconds remaining in the game.

44:04.725 --> 44:07.102
[suspenseful music continues]

44:09.688 --> 44:10.856
[Usagi grunts]

44:11.690 --> 44:13.484
[Aguni grunts]

44:17.696 --> 44:19.615
- [gunshots]
- [announcer] 20 seconds.

44:20.491 --> 44:21.533
[strains]

44:21.617 --> 44:23.911
[grunts]

44:27.623 --> 44:29.625
[groans]

44:31.210 --> 44:32.044
You called?

44:32.127 --> 44:33.295
[announcer] Ten seconds.

44:33.379 --> 44:34.380
[gunshots]

44:34.463 --> 44:36.382
- [Chishiya] Here!
- [taser crackling]

44:36.465 --> 44:37.549
[grunts]

44:38.801 --> 44:40.344
[taser crackling]

44:43.222 --> 44:44.306
[announcer] Five.

44:44.390 --> 44:45.641
- Four.
- [Arisu] The buttons!

44:45.724 --> 44:46.934
[announcer] Three.

44:47.017 --> 44:49.061
Two. One.

44:49.144 --> 44:50.521
[clanks]

44:50.604 --> 44:51.730
[coughs]

44:52.439 --> 44:53.357
[gasps]

44:53.440 --> 44:55.192
EMERGENCY BUTTON
STOP

45:00.030 --> 45:01.573
[phone chiming]

45:02.616 --> 45:06.161
[announcer] Game cleared. Congratulations.

45:16.672 --> 45:17.714
[breathes nervously]

45:20.342 --> 45:23.387
[sobbing]

45:23.470 --> 45:24.388
[woman gasps]

45:25.222 --> 45:26.181
[woman breathes shakily]

45:28.392 --> 45:30.477
[device warbling, pinging]

45:32.729 --> 45:34.565
[beeping rapidly]

45:34.648 --> 45:35.607
Oh, no.

45:35.691 --> 45:36.900
- [explosion]
- [spluttering]

45:36.984 --> 45:38.318
[both wince]

45:44.366 --> 45:48.745
[both breathing heavily]

45:53.125 --> 45:55.169
[Karube grunts]

45:56.628 --> 45:57.754
[groans]

45:57.838 --> 45:59.715
[panting]

46:02.885 --> 46:04.887
[gun clicking]

46:17.399 --> 46:18.525
So this guy…

46:19.693 --> 46:21.778
had no choice but to play the game?

46:28.494 --> 46:29.912
[sighs]

46:30.704 --> 46:32.706
[man on radio] Are you there? Over.

46:34.333 --> 46:35.918
Do you copy?

46:36.710 --> 46:38.378
Repeat. Are you there?

46:38.462 --> 46:39.505
[metal clunks]

46:39.588 --> 46:42.466
[Karube groans]

46:42.549 --> 46:44.760
[man on radio] Please respond. Over.

46:46.762 --> 46:48.680
[patting, rubbing]

46:49.306 --> 46:52.643
[man on radio] Do you copy?
Answer. Over. Do you read?

46:52.726 --> 46:54.144
…it's in our hands now.

46:54.228 --> 46:55.187
[radio flicks off]

46:55.771 --> 46:56.939
"Answer"?

46:59.149 --> 47:00.526
[Karube] Hey, can you hear me?

47:02.069 --> 47:04.196
Hey, what "answer"?

47:04.696 --> 47:06.323
[radio flicks on, static]

47:06.406 --> 47:07.658
[man on radio] Come back.

47:07.741 --> 47:10.536
The answer is in our hands now.

47:11.703 --> 47:13.747
Get back to the Beach.

47:13.830 --> 47:14.998
[radio flicks off]

47:15.082 --> 47:16.250
[Karube] "The Beach"?

47:16.833 --> 47:18.835
[suspenseful music]

47:19.586 --> 47:21.588
[winces]

47:23.632 --> 47:25.634
[breathing deeply]

47:28.345 --> 47:29.888
[radio flicks on]

47:29.972 --> 47:31.056
[man on radio] Get back.

47:31.932 --> 47:33.934
Get back to the Beach.

47:35.269 --> 47:37.854
- Get back to the Beach!
- [radio flicks off]

47:42.317 --> 47:44.403
[closing theme music]
